WHAT A1 BOUGHT.  Every family the two earlier arms damaged is repaired.
TRANSVERSE is now BELOW the battery on all three (CYXY 63->4, HECA
95->63, SPJC 46->51 near-flat) — the transect rows and the 5 % interior
law together hold the corridor.  STEPS are gone (SPJC 37->0, HECA
192->8).  The surface is far closer to the battery than v1's: worst
airside |dz| CYXY 3.95->0.93 m, SPJC 9.66->1.09 m, HECA 18.23->6.77 m.
CYXY clears its bar by 59 and its within_shape airside is ZERO; the
service_junction spine 37.1 % row that survived apronpop AND v1 is GONE
(0 rows within 30 m of 60.712398,-135.077719).

THE STOPS — AND THE ATTRIBUTION IS THE SAME ON BOTH AIRPORTS.

  NOT ONE VIOLATION IS PRICED BY THE NEW 5 % INTERIOR CAP.
    SPJC within_shape airside 52 = 46 @cap 1.0 % + 6 @cap 1.5 % + 0 @5 %.
    HECA within_shape airside 1383 = 1326 @1.0 % + 56 @1.5 % + 1 @8 % + 0 @5 %.
  The interior law mints nothing; it is doing its job.  The residual debt
  sits entirely on the STRICT class — the movement surfaces and, above
  all, the RING-ADJACENT branch A1 §1a deliberately reserved for the
  strict cap (R19-5's catch).

  HECA, the bigger STOP (+112).  within_shape apron|apron airside 1089
  (battery) -> 1258 (v2).  Of those 1258, 582 are frontage CHORDS and 676
  are GENERIC — and since no row anywhere carries the 5 % cap, every
  violating generic row is necessarily RING-ADJACENT (the only way to be
  generic and strict under A1) or foreign-priced (28 of the 676, by
  junction / service laws).  So ~648 rows are apron RING EDGES over the
  strict 1 % cap.  Severity moved with them: the >2x-cap class 447 -> 663,
  accumulated excess 4332 -> 4564 percentage-points, worst 33.8 % -> 57.8 %
  at SPJC and the HECA head now at 1.11-1.64 % against a 1.00 % cap on
  7.2-7.6 m chords.  Sites, HECA head: (30.11843,31.41048),
  (30.11848,31.41047), (30.11845,31.41048), (30.12442,31.41397).

  SPJC (+15), family by family vs the battery: within_shape +7 (45->52),
  transverse +5 (46->51), frontage_near_miss +2 (0->2), plane_gradient +1.
  strip_arc (54), drainage_spine (36) and strip_longitudinal (7) are
  UNCHANGED.  The worst NEW airside rows are apron|apron on way -10113 at
  1.016-1.033 % against a 1.000 % cap — hairline in grade, large in metres
  because the chords are ~260 m.  19 of the 52 sit within 1.25x of cap.
  Sites: (-12.020149,-77.110458), (-12.020133,-77.110446),
  (-12.019231,-77.110059).

  MECHANISM (one sentence): the 5 % interior is a much better constraint
  than no constraint, but it is still four points looser than the strict
  cap, so the interior may legally tilt under the transect rows and the
  movement surfaces and ring edges bounding it absorb the difference —
  the same shape as the v1 failure, one order of magnitude smaller.
  NO FIX ATTEMPTED (attempt 2 of the population spec; the brief's
  instruction is STOP + attribution).

