  The new cap lockstep twin found a PRE-EXISTING reader drift and does not
  adopt it: one ring edge reads the blend branch's 1.5 % in the bake and
  the plain body cap in the census, identically with the flag on and off.
  The twin asserts NO NEW drift rather than zero drift.

BUILD HYGIENE.  Three v2 builds, all rc=0, all "shared repo UNCHANGED".
No --no-ledger, no degraded-DEM override, no timing claim.

OWNER QUESTIONS THIS LANE DOCKETS
  1. THE RING-ADJACENT BRANCH is where HECA's remaining debt lives (~648
     rows).  A1 §1a reserved it for the strict cap on R19-5 grounds.  Is a
     long apron RING EDGE a movement surface (strict) or interior (5 %)?
     The measurement says the answer decides HECA's bar.
  2. A role-LESS duplicate ring of an apron host is priced at the strict
     cap while its host prices its interior at 5 % — one geometry, two
     laws (test_harness duplicate-ring twin).
  3. The blend-branch cap drift between census and bake (pre-existing).
  4. broken_by_emit at 48-62 % — the "nothing moves after the final
     projection" spec A1 §8d exists to trigger.
  5. SPLP / KAFW / KDFW have no arm under this tree.
